late(279.724805 101.8275) scale(0.075 -0.075)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-3d\" d=\"M 1184 2573 L 1670 2573 Q 2125 2573 2352 2784 Q 2579 2995 2579 3315 L 2579 3360 Q 2579 3712 2358 3888 Q 2138 4064 1779 4064 Q 1434 4064 1216 3913 Q 998 3763 858 3507 L 461 3814 Q 576 3994 749 4160 Q 922 4326 1178 4435 Q 1434 4544 1792 4544 Q 2170 4544 2477 4413 Q 2784 4282 2966 4032 Q 3149 3782 3149 3418 Q 3149 2989 2899 2726 Q 2650 2464 2291 2374 L 2291 2349 Q 2534 2304 2748 2166 Q 2963 2029 3097 1795 Q 3232 1562 3232 1222 Q 3232 838 3043 547 Q 2854 256 2512 89 Q 2170 -77 1715 -77 Q 1331 -77 1059 35 Q 787 147 598 320 Q 410 493 269 685 L 672 992 Q 845 730 1072 566 Q 1299 403 1709 403 Q 2182 403 2425 620 Q 2669 838 2669 1229 L 2669 1280 Q 2669 1677 2425 1891 Q 2182 2106 1709 2106 L 1184 2106 L 1184 2573 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3d\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_23\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(324.654675 72.8475) scale(0.075 -0.075)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-40\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_24\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(369.584545 43.8675) scale(0.075 -0.075)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-43\" d=\"M 3411 2829 Q 3411 2330 3267 1894 Q 3123 1459 2883 1094 Q 2643 730 2364 451 Q 2086 173 1818 0 L 1126 0 Q 1606 352 1945 685 Q 2285 1018 2509 1408 Q 2733 1798 2854 2317 L 2822 2330 Q 2720 2150 2573 2003 Q 2426 1856 2224 1773 Q 2022 1690 1747 1690 Q 1363 1690 1065 1856 Q 768 2022 598 2332 Q 429 2643 429 3066 Q 429 3507 614 3840 Q 800 4173 1133 4358 Q 1466 4544 1914 4544 Q 2381 4544 2713 4336 Q 3046 4128 3228 3744 Q 3411 3360 3411 2829 z\nM 1920 2144 Q 2214 2144 2422 2253 Q 2630 2362 2742 2573 Q 2854 2784 2854 3085 L 2854 3136 Q 2854 3437 2742 3648 Q 2630 3859 2422 3968 Q 2214 4077 1920 4077 Q 1626 4077 1418 3968 Q 1210 3859 1098 3648 Q 986 3437 986 3136 L 986 3085 Q 986 2784 1098 2573 Q 1210 2362 1418 2253 Q 1626 2144 1920 2144 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-43\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p01c09ea69b\"><rect x=\"46.1\" y=\"15.0915\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Subscribers around the last price rise (k)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Subscribers fell about 8% over three months, from 152k to 140k, then recovered most of the loss within five months.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> customers react, but the core audience stays. The real risk is the short-term dip, not a permanent loss.</p>"},{"q":"If 10% of subscribers cancel, does the rise pay off? How many could cancel before it stops paying?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Monthly margin today: 180k × ($6.99 − $1.50) = <b>$988k</b>.</p> <p>After: 162k × ($8.49 − $1.50) = <b>$1,132k</b>, +$144k a month (about $1.7M a year).</p> <p>Break-even loss: 1 − 5.49 ÷ 6.99 = <b>21.5%</b>. Paloma can lose about 1 in 5 subscribers and still be no worse off.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> with last time's dip of about 8%, there's a wide safety margin.</p>"},{"q":"How would you roll it out?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Explain why</b>: more films, restored classics, better subtitles</li> <li><b>Annual plan</b> at a modest discount (e.g. $89 a year, about 13% off 12 × $8.49, and still above today's $83.88) to lock in loyal subscribers</li> <li><b>Keep existing subscribers at the old price for three months</b> to soften the dip</li> <li><b>Watch new sign-ups</b>, not just cancellations: the higher price may slow growth</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Raise the price to $8.49. Even if 10% of subscribers cancel, monthly margin rises by about $144k, and the rise only stops paying if more than 21.5% leave; last time the dip was about 8% and mostly recovered. Pair it with an annual plan and a three-month grace period for existing subscribers. Risk: slower sign-ups from new viewers. Next step: track cancellations and sign-ups weekly for three months after launch.","great":["Reads the chart for both the dip and the recovery","Computes break-even churn, not just one scenario","Thinks about sign-ups as well as cancellations","Proposes a rollout that softens the reaction"],"id":35,"slug":"paloma-streaming"}